# CMakePresets.json board defaults: Seeed reTerminal Sticky
# Sets the hardware model and IDF target used by the "seeed_reterminal_sticky" preset.

CONFIG_IDF_TARGET="esp32s3"
CONFIG_DRAFTLING_MODEL_SEEED_RETERMINAL_STICKY=y

# 32 MB flash (ESP32-S3R8, per Seeed's hardware-overview page), unlike
# the 16 MB default in sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3.
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_32MB=y

# Use a dual-OTA partition table (with an "otadata" partition) instead
# of the shared single-"factory" partitions.csv, matching the Xteink
# X4 Pro / Classic rationale: this board also runs the third-party
# "Crosspoint" firmware (built with PlatformIO/Arduino-esp32, which
# expects an OTA-capable table), so keeping one here lets the device
# move to Crosspoint -- or back to it -- without first re-flashing a
# partition table over the serial port. See
# partitions_seeed_reterminal_sticky.csv.
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions_seeed_reterminal_sticky.csv"

# No "SD card via USB" support on this board: per Seeed's hardware
# overview and the FreeInk SDK, the case's USB-C port is bridged
# through an on-board WCH USB-to-UART chip onto UART0, not wired to
# the ESP32-S3's native USB-OTG peripheral (whose D+/D- pins, GPIO19/
# 20, this board instead uses for its PDM microphone). CONFIG_TINYUSB_
# MSC_ENABLED is therefore left unset, unlike every other e-paper
# board's sdkconfig.defaults.<board>.
